# dbt Naming Contracts

## Model Prefixes

| Layer | Prefix | Folder | Example |
|-------|--------|--------|---------|
| Staging | `stg_` | `models/staging/` | `stg_issues.sql` |
| Intermediate | `int_` | `models/intermediate/` | `int_issue_status_history.sql` |
| Facts | `fct_` | `models/marts/` | `fct_daily_status.sql` |
| Dimensions | `dim_` | `models/marts/` | `dim_users.sql` |
| Marts (general) | none | `models/marts/` | `issue_status_as_of.sql` |

## Conventions

- **snake_case** for all names (models, columns, macros)
- **Pluralize entities**: `stg_issues` not `stg_issue`
- **Descriptive intermediate**: `int_issue_status_history` not `int_issues_v2`

## YAML Files

| Type | Pattern | Example |
|------|---------|---------|
| Model docs | `_<folder>.yml` | `_staging.yml` |
| Sources | `__sources.yml` | `__sources.yml` |

## Column Naming

```sql
-- ✅ GOOD: Clear, consistent
issue_key, status, created_at, updated_at

-- ❌ BAD: Inconsistent, unclear
issueKey, Status, createdDate, update_ts
```

## Anti-Patterns

```
❌ stg_jira_issues.sql     -- Don't include source system in staging name
✅ stg_issues.sql          -- Source system defined in __sources.yml

❌ int_temp_issues.sql     -- No temp/v2/final suffixes
✅ int_issue_transitions.sql

❌ final_report.sql        -- No generic names
✅ issue_status_as_of.sql  -- Descriptive purpose
```
